# Claude Workflow configuration reference
#
# Use `claude-workflow config` for common model, reasoning, and permission
# settings. This file documents advanced and provider-specific overrides.
#
# Put trusted user-wide overrides in ~/.claude-workflow.env. The legacy
# ~/.ultrathink.env file is read afterward for upgrade compatibility.
# Keep blank compatibility aliases written by `claude-workflow config`; they
# intentionally shadow stale values with the same name in the legacy file.
# Per-session workflow entrypoints deliberately ignore a repository .env unless
# the parent shell exports CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_LOAD_PROJECT_ENV=true. Shared mode
# rejects this opt-in because its daemon is not repository-scoped.

# Main/frontier route. Fable 5.1 exposes its 1M context through the canonical API
# model ID, so no client-only suffix is required.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_MAIN_MODEL_ID=claude-fable-5-1
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_MAIN_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_MAIN_UPSTREAM_MODEL=claude-fable-5-1
# Leave passthrough unset to include the main family and native fallback targets.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_PASSTHROUGH_MODELS=claude-fable-5-1*,claude-opus-5,claude-opus-5[1m],claude-opus-4-8,claude-opus-4-8[1m]
# `claude-workflow config --main codex` instead exposes the concise client model
# `codex-astra` by default and routes the main session through
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_MODEL and ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT
# below. The same two settings control workflow agents.

# Raw route selector used before the launcher derives a concise truthful
# Claude-facing ID after all route-map overrides are resolved.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_SUBAGENT_MODEL_ID=codex-astra
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_SUBAGENT_UPSTREAM_MODEL=gpt-6-astra
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_SUBAGENT_REASONING_EFFORT=max
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_SUBAGENT_VERBOSITY=high
# False preserves the concise requested ID in response metadata. Set true only
# when a client explicitly wants the longer provider/model/effort description.
# CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_DISPLAY_ROUTED_MODEL=false
# Leave this unset so the launcher derives codex-astra, codex-gpt-5.4, or the
# matching truthful ID. A set value is an operator-owned route ID, not a
# cosmetic display label.
# CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_MODEL_ID=codex-astra

# Permission bypass is the intentional launcher default. Use it only in trusted
# repositories and machine environments. Set false to restore Claude prompts.
# CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_SKIP_PERMISSIONS=false
# This opt-in must be exported by the parent shell; a project .env cannot enable itself.
# CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_LOAD_PROJECT_ENV=false

# Per-launch workflow gateway. Leave the port unset/0 for an isolated dynamic
# launcher port. A raw long-running gateway requires a positive port and
# defaults to 4319; the managed daemon defaults to 4318.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_PORT=0
# The shell daemon manager reads these values from its parent environment before
# the Node gateway loads this file. Export manager overrides in your shell rc;
# use absolute paths or $HOME rather than a literal ~ inside a variable value.
# export ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_DAEMON_PORT=4318
# export CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_GATEWAY_STATE_DIR="$HOME/.cache/claude-workflow"
# export CLAUDE_WORKFLOW_GATEWAY_ENV_FILE="$HOME/.cache/claude-workflow/claude-workflow-gateway.env"

# Non-loopback binds require gateway authentication. With a shared secret, a
# dedicated Anthropic key is also required for every Anthropic route because
# the inbound Claude credential is consumed by the gateway. A generic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not accepted for this shared-secret role.
# Generate a 256-bit value with
# `node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"`,
# then paste it here.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_SHARED_SECRET=<generated_64_hex_character_secret>
# Invalid gateway credentials are limited per source address. Valid credentials,
# no-secret loopback requests, and anonymous health polling do not consume this
# quota. The concurrency cap is held until each model response or stream closes.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_AUTH_FAILURE_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_AUTH_FAILURE_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=60
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=32
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_VERSION=2023-06-01

# Optional Kimi K3 main route. The `config --main kimi` preset selects exact K3
# at 1048576 tokens and requires Allegretto or higher. Then put the API key in
# ~/.claude-workflow.env and keep that file mode 0600.
# The dedicated gateway key wins over the KIMI_API_KEY compatibility fallback.
# Kimi Code and Kimi Open Platform credentials are not interchangeable.
# Custom remote endpoints must use HTTPS. HTTP is accepted only on loopback;
# redirects are rejected so the credential stays on the configured origin.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_KIMI_API_KEY=your_kimi_code_api_key
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_KIMI_BASE_URL=https://api.kimi.com/coding/
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_KIMI_MODEL=k3
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_KIMI_REASONING_EFFORT=max
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_KIMI_CONTEXT_TOKENS=1048576
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_KIMI_VERSION=2023-06-01
# Moderato supports K3 at 256K; select it with `config --main k3`.
# Workflow launchers generate local gateway authentication for non-Anthropic
# main routes. Equivalent custom raw-gateway routes must set
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_SHARED_SECRET.
# Set ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_PASSTHROUGH_MODELS=none for a raw Kimi-only
# gateway; mixed Kimi/Anthropic routes require ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# The launcher derives CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW and
# CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS from the resolved main and delegated routes.
# Native Claude effort is separate: use /effort ultracode with Fable. The
# launcher clears stale CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL pins except for Kimi/Qwen's
# required client profiles. Canonical Anthropic IDs ignore the custom maximum,
# but Claude's proactive compaction threshold is shared. Do not set these
# derived client values directly.

# Optional Alibaba Qwen 3.8 Max main route. `config --main qwen` selects the
# exact qwen3.8-max model. Alibaba documents a 1000000-token context window,
# 983616-token maximum input in thinking mode, 131072-token maximum output, and
# 262144-token maximum chain of thought. This route uses 983616 as its safe input
# ceiling and selects xhigh reasoning. Store the sk-sp- Token Plan key in the
# owner-only ~/.claude-workflow.env file.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_QWEN_API_KEY=your_sk_sp_token_plan_key
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_QWEN_BASE_URL=https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_QWEN_MODEL=qwen3.8-max
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_QWEN_REASONING_EFFORT=xhigh
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_QWEN_CONTEXT_TOKENS=983616
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_QWEN_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=131072
# BAILIAN_TOKEN_PLAN_API_KEY and QWEN_API_KEY are compatibility aliases. A
# generic DASHSCOPE_API_KEY is accepted only with an explicit matching
# QWEN_BASE_URL. This profile does not accept the /apps/anthropic endpoint and
# rejects redirects so the credential stays on the configured origin.

# Codex app-server route. The command is the executable only; the gateway adds
# `app-server`. Claude Workflow requires Codex CLI 0.153.4 or newer and starts
# isolated workflow threads with no optional native execution environment.
# Codex 0.153.4 still exposes its built-in code-mode exec/wait control wrappers;
# repository operations use Claude Code's dynamic tools.
# An owner-only per-process catalog snapshot suppresses model-enabled native
# async-question and clock tools. Restart the gateway to refresh that metadata.
# Shared setup fails if cwd-relative PATH entries select a different Codex
# executable from the managed state directory. Use an absolute command path for
# a repository-local install or wrapper.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_ENABLED=true
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_COMMAND=codex
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_CWD=/absolute/path/to/project
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_SANDBOX=workspace-write
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_APPROVAL_POLICY=never
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-astra
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT=max
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_VERBOSITY=low

# Context/session limits. `long` asks the installed Codex model catalog for its
# advertised maximum; `standard` uses its normal window. The workflow default is
# `long`. An exact raw-window request is clamped to the catalog maximum.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_CONTEXT=long
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_CONTEXT_WINDOW=872000
# Set 0 to use the capability-derived safe input budget and native compaction.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_INPUT_MAX_TOKENS=0
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_AUTO_COMPACT_TOKEN_LIMIT=0
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_AUTO_COMPACT_TOKEN_LIMIT_SCOPE=total
# Workflow sessions default both generic byte caps to 0 so the installed Codex
# app-server owns token-aware tool-output truncation. Positive values opt back
# into generic transport caps; the verified contiguous Read-page guard remains
# active independently.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_TOOL_RESULT_MAX_BYTES=0
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_TOOL_RESULT_WINDOW_MAX_BYTES=0
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_FORK_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_PENDING_TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_CODEX_MAX_SESSIONS=16

# Optional tracing. For the shared daemon, export the trace directory from the
# parent shell because the shell manager selects it before this file is loaded.
# Use an absolute path or off/false/no/0. Existing custom directories must be
# mode 0700; trace files are mode 0600 and rotate at 8 MiB / three files.
# export ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_TRACE_DIR="$HOME/.cache/claude-workflow/gateway-trace"
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_TRACE_MAX_BYTES=8388608
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_TRACE_MAX_FILES=3

# Optional OpenAI-compatible provider profile for an explicit raw route map.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_OPENAI_MODEL=your-approved-openai-model
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_OPENAI_VERBOSITY=low

# Optional DeepSeek provider profile for an explicit raw route map.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your_deepseek_api_key
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_DEEPSEEK_REASONING_EFFORT=max

# Optional GLM/Z.ai provider profile for an explicit raw route map.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_GLM_API_KEY=your_zai_api_key
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_GLM_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_GLM_MODEL=glm-5.2
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_GLM_REASONING_EFFORT=max
# ULTRATHINK_THINKING_LEVEL=HIGH

# Exact entries win over wildcard route-map entries. Exact entries also become
# the default /v1/models discovery list.
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_ROUTE_MAP_JSON='{"codex-astra":{"provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-astra","sandbox":"workspace-write","approvalPolicy":"never","reasoningEffort":"max","verbosity":"high","displayName":"Codex Astra"}}'
# ULTRATHINK_GATEWAY_EXPOSED_MODELS=claude-fable-5-1,codex-astra

# Corporate proxy support. The launcher adds its local host to NO_PROXY/no_proxy.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:8080
# HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:8080
# ALL_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:8080
# NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1
